# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# our working notes — internal, not part of the submission
#
# These are how the build was run, not how the game works. The plan, the
# progress log and the agent instructions carry competitor notes and
# scheduling that has no business in a public repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
MASTER-PLAN.md
PROGRESS.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
ART.md

# CASES.md is the answer key. It says in plain English which six photos are
# evidence, which are traps and why. Shipping it hands a reader the solution
# before they ever play.
CASES.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# working art
#
# Raw model downloads, unprocessed generations, contact sheets and concept
# art — 260MB+ of source material that never ships. Everything the game
# actually loads lives in public/ and IS committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
/art-raw

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# throwaway from driving the browser
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
/.playwright-mcp
/room-*.png
/lab-*.png
/gpt-*.png
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT ignored, on purpose:
#
#   CREDITS.md       most of the 3D models are CC BY, which requires
#                    attribution. This file has to ship with the code.
#   README.md        the challenge scores it directly.
#   public/models    the game cannot load without them.
#   public/cases     the 14 case photos and case.json.
#   public/room      cork, window view, posters.
#   public/textures  wall and floor.
#   scripts/         how every asset was made and processed — part of
#                    showing the work.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
